  "raw_meta_yaml": "schema_version: 1\n\ncontext:\n  # ahrs uses PEP 604 union syntax (str | int) at import time, which requires Python >=3.10.\n  python_min: \"3.10\"\n  version: \"0.4.0\"\n\npackage:\n  name: ahrs\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://pypi.org/packages/source/a/ahrs/ahrs-${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: 4b632b9e53b9cfd1cecadefa543a3534574baeafeef048db703ab33a07dcca21\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n  noarch: python\n  script: ${{ PYTHON }} -m pip install . -vv --no-deps --no-build-isolation\n\nrequirements:\n  host:\n    - python ${{ python_min }}.*\n    - hatchling\n    - pip\n  run:\n    - python >=${{ python_min }}\n    - numpy >=1.17\n    - docutils >=0.18.1\n\ntests:\n  - python:\n      imports:\n        - ahrs\n      pip_check: true\n      python_version: ${{ python_min }}.*\n\nabout:\n  summary: Attitude and Heading Reference Systems.\n  description: |\n    AHRS is a collection of attitude estimators and utilities for working\n    with orientations in Python, built on NumPy. It implements many sensor\n    fusion filters (Madgwick, Mahony, EKF, complementary, and more) to\n    estimate orientation from gyroscope, accelerometer, and magnetometer\n    readings, along with tools for quaternions, rotation matrices, and\n    world geomagnetic/gravity models.\n  license: MIT\n  license_file: LICENSE\n  homepage: https://github.com/Mayitzin/ahrs/\n  repository: https://github.com/Mayitzin/ahrs/\n  documentation: https://ahrs.readthedocs.io/\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - ruben-arts\n",
